1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:15,996
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is May twenty-eighth. Today's story is about aviation: a Japanese airline just launched its first flight with a brand-new airplane. Let's listen.

2
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:27,995
[News] 今日、スカイマークは新しい飛行機「ボーイング737-8」の初めての便を飛ばしました。

3
00:00:28,696 --> 00:00:43,264
[News] 朝7時35分に羽田空港を出発して、福岡空港に向かいました。日本の航空会社がこの飛行機を使うのは初めてです。

4
00:00:43,963 --> 00:00:54,043
[News] この飛行機は、今まで使っていた飛行機より燃料を約15パーセント少なく使うことができます。

5
00:00:54,743 --> 00:01:02,207
[News] 二酸化炭素の排出量も減るので、環境にやさしいと言われています。

6
00:01:02,908 --> 00:01:12,676
[News] 機内には充電ポートやコンセントがあり、乗客はスマートフォンやパソコンを充電できます。

7
00:01:13,376 --> 00:01:23,743
[News] 騒音が今までの飛行機より50パーセント少なく、パイロットも「静かすぎる」と驚いています。

8
00:01:24,444 --> 00:01:33,780
[News] スカイマークは合計20機を注文しており、これから他の路線にも広げていく予定です。

9
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:36,111
[Host] Let's break it down.

10
00:01:36,712 --> 00:01:38,272
[Host] The opening line.

11
00:01:38,871 --> 00:01:44,751
[Slow] 新しい飛行機の初めての便を飛ばしました。

12
00:01:45,552 --> 00:01:48,599
[Host] They flew the first flight of the new airplane.

13
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,120
[Vocab] 便

14
00:01:51,519 --> 00:02:01,695
[Host] Flight, or scheduled service. You'll see this word at airports and train stations. First flight, last flight. It counts transportation services.

15
00:02:02,296 --> 00:02:04,168
[Host] A first for Japan.

16
00:02:04,768 --> 00:02:11,800
[Slow] 日本の航空会社がこの飛行機を使うのは初めてです。

17
00:02:12,599 --> 00:02:17,039
[Host] This is the first time a Japanese airline has used this airplane.

18
00:02:17,639 --> 00:02:20,544
[Vocab] 航空会社

19
00:02:20,943 --> 00:02:29,391
[Host] Airline. The first two characters mean aviation. The last two mean company. Put them together and you get airline.

20
00:02:29,991 --> 00:02:32,271
[Host] Why this airplane is special.

21
00:02:32,872 --> 00:02:42,592
[Slow] 今まで使っていた飛行機より燃料を約15パーセント少なく使うことができます。

22
00:02:43,391 --> 00:02:47,807
[Host] It can use about fifteen percent less fuel than the airplane they used before.

23
00:02:48,407 --> 00:02:50,783
[Vocab] 燃料

24
00:02:51,183 --> 00:03:01,000
[Host] Fuel. The first character means to burn. The second means material. Burning material. Cars, planes, they all need this.

25
00:03:01,599 --> 00:03:03,183
[Host] Good for the planet.

26
00:03:03,783 --> 00:03:08,319
[Slow] 環境にやさしいと言われています。

27
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:14,711
[Host] It is said to be environmentally friendly. You'll hear this phrase a lot in Japanese news.

28
00:03:15,312 --> 00:03:17,687
[Vocab] 環境

29
00:03:18,087 --> 00:03:25,936
[Host] Environment. One of the most common words in news about climate and sustainability. Very useful to know.

30
00:03:26,536 --> 00:03:28,647
[Host] What's new for passengers.

31
00:03:29,247 --> 00:03:35,872
[Slow] 乗客はスマートフォンやパソコンを充電できます。

32
00:03:36,671 --> 00:03:40,367
[Host] Passengers can charge their smartphones and computers.

33
00:03:40,967 --> 00:03:43,415
[Vocab] 乗客

34
00:03:43,816 --> 00:03:54,472
[Host] Passenger. The first character means to ride. The second means guest. A riding guest. You'll see it on buses, trains, and planes.

35
00:03:55,072 --> 00:03:57,280
[Vocab] 充電

36
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:08,048
[Host] Charging. The first character means to fill. The second means electricity. Fill with electricity. You probably do this every day with your phone.

37
00:04:08,647 --> 00:04:10,903
[Host] And it's surprisingly quiet.

38
00:04:11,503 --> 00:04:19,184
[Slow] 騒音が今までの飛行機より50パーセント少なくなりました。

39
00:04:19,983 --> 00:04:28,216
[Host] Noise has been reduced by fifty percent compared to previous airplanes. Even the pilots say it's too quiet in the cockpit.

40
00:04:28,815 --> 00:04:31,120
[Vocab] 騒音

41
00:04:31,519 --> 00:04:40,567
[Host] Noise. The first character means noisy. The second means sound. Unwanted sound. The opposite of music.

42
00:04:41,168 --> 00:04:44,168
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

43
00:04:44,767 --> 00:04:56,168
[News] 今日、スカイマークは新しい飛行機「ボーイング737-8」の初めての便を飛ばしました。

44
00:04:56,867 --> 00:05:11,435
[News] 朝7時35分に羽田空港を出発して、福岡空港に向かいました。日本の航空会社がこの飛行機を使うのは初めてです。

45
00:05:12,136 --> 00:05:22,216
[News] この飛行機は、今まで使っていた飛行機より燃料を約15パーセント少なく使うことができます。

46
00:05:22,915 --> 00:05:30,379
[News] 二酸化炭素の排出量も減るので、環境にやさしいと言われています。

47
00:05:31,079 --> 00:05:40,848
[News] 機内には充電ポートやコンセントがあり、乗客はスマートフォンやパソコンを充電できます。

48
00:05:41,548 --> 00:05:51,915
[News] 騒音が今までの飛行機より50パーセント少なく、パイロットも「静かすぎる」と驚いています。

49
00:05:52,615 --> 00:06:01,951
[News] スカイマークは合計20機を注文しており、これから他の路線にも広げていく予定です。

50
00:06:02,651 --> 00:06:05,387
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

51
00:06:05,987 --> 00:06:10,427
[Slow] この飛行機の名前は何ですか？

52
00:06:11,228 --> 00:06:16,052
[Host] What is the name of this airplane? Boeing seven thirty-seven dash eight.

53
00:06:16,651 --> 00:06:21,740
[Slow] 燃料はどのくらい少なくなりましたか？

54
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:27,459
[Host] How much less fuel does it use? About fifteen percent less than before.

55
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:31,755
[Slow] 機内で何ができますか？

56
00:06:32,555 --> 00:06:37,355
[Host] What can you do inside the cabin? You can charge your smartphone or computer.

57
00:06:37,956 --> 00:06:50,339
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

58
00:06:50,939 --> 00:06:53,196
[News] また明日。
